    "compliance.check_nis2_admin_mfa_title": "MFA on every admin account",
    "compliance.check_nis2_admin_mfa_desc": "NIS2 Art. 21(2)(j) expects multi-factor authentication for privileged access. Every organisation admin must have TOTP enabled or sign in through an SSO provider that enforces MFA.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_admin_mfa_fix": "Ask each listed admin to enable MFA under their account settings, or enforce MFA at your identity provider and confirm it under Compliance → Settings.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_policy_coverage_title": "Security policies cover every Art. 21 measure",
    "compliance.check_nis2_policy_coverage_desc": "Each of the ten Art. 21(2) measures must be backed by a published, current policy. The check maps the measures to the ISMS policy set under Compliance → Policies.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_policy_coverage_fix": "Publish the missing policies and complete overdue reviews under Compliance → Policies.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_risk_analysis_title": "Risk analysis maintained",
    "compliance.check_nis2_risk_analysis_desc": "A current risk register with owners and treatments is the first Art. 21(2) measure. An empty register or overdue reviews mean risks are not being managed.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_risk_analysis_fix": "Add or review risks under Compliance → Risks and record a treatment for every high risk.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_effectiveness_review_title": "Effectiveness of measures assessed",
    "compliance.check_nis2_effectiveness_review_desc": "Art. 21(2)(f) requires assessing whether the measures work: an internal audit or management review in the last year plus continuous check sweeps.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_effectiveness_review_fix": "Record an internal audit or management review under Compliance → Audits and keep the scheduled check sweeps running.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_training_title": "Cyber-hygiene training and policy acknowledgement",
    "compliance.check_nis2_training_desc": "Staff must acknowledge the security policies and receive basic cyber-hygiene training (Art. 21(2)(g), Art. 20(2)). Coverage counts current policy acknowledgements and training attestations from the last year.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_training_fix": "Ask staff to acknowledge the published policies and record external training under Compliance → Training.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_board_approval_title": "Management approved the security policy",
    "compliance.check_nis2_board_approval_desc": "Art. 20 makes management accountable: the information-security policy must be published and acknowledged by every organisation admin, and management must follow cybersecurity training (recorded as an attestation).",
    "compliance.check_nis2_board_approval_fix": "Publish the information-security policy and have every admin acknowledge it under Compliance → Policies; stamp the management training date under Compliance → Settings.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_early_warning_title": "24-hour early-warning path operational",
    "compliance.check_nis2_early_warning_desc": "Significant incidents need an early warning within 24 hours, a notification within 72 hours and a final report within a month (Art. 23). The incident register tracks all three clocks; the platform never files on your behalf, so each report is recorded as a stamp.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_early_warning_fix": "Configure the authority channel, CSIRT contact and notification recipients under Compliance → Settings, and record each report on the incident under Compliance → Incidents.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_registration_title": "Entity registered with the authority",
    "compliance.check_nis2_registration_desc": "Essential and important entities must register with the national authority. The registration lives outside the platform, so this check records your self-classification and the registration reference and date as an attestation.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_registration_fix": "Set your NIS2 classification and, when in scope, the registration reference and date under Compliance → Settings.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_questionnaire_pack_title": "Supplier questionnaire pack ready",
    "compliance.check_nis2_questionnaire_pack_desc": "Customers in NIS2 scope send supplier questionnaires. The ISO evidence bundle answers them when the supplier, incident, continuity and security policies are published, the SoA is seeded and the check results are fresh. This check never fails: not having exported the bundle is not a control failure.",
    "compliance.check_nis2_questionnaire_pack_fix": "Publish the listed policies under Compliance → Policies, seed the SoA under Compliance → SoA and download the evidence bundle from the Reports tab.",
    "compliance.fw_gdpr_name": "GDPR",
    "compliance.fw_gdpr_desc": "Lawful, transparent and secure processing of personal data; rights of data subjects, breach notification within 72 hours, accountability.",
    "compliance.fw_gdpr_affects": "every processing of personal data in your organisation — the Digital Omnibus has not been adopted for the data/privacy part, so nothing softens.",
    "compliance.fw_gdpr_phase_in_force": "in force",
    "compliance.fw_aia_name": "AI Act",
    "compliance.fw_aia_desc": "Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 · Omnibus: Art. 4 \"support\" instead of \"ensure\", Annex III moved to Dec 2027",
    "compliance.fw_aia_affects": "every customer-facing agent and every routine that generates content — disclose that it is AI, mark generated output machine-readably.",
